% A limit that refuses a relation the Magic rewrite generated names the
% predicate the program wrote, which is what a reader can change.  The
% query's binding of path's first argument is answered through path$bf,
% which holds part of path, and the refusal names path/2.
edge(a, b). edge(b, c). edge(c, d). edge(d, e).
path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).
path(a, X)?
